```java
public static Number createNumber(String str) {
    if (str == null || str.isEmpty()) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Input string cannot be null or empty");
    }

    // Check for hexadecimal strings
    if (str.startsWith("0x") || str.startsWith("-0x")) {
        return Integer.parseInt(str, 16);
    }

    char lastChar = str.charAt(str.length() - 1);
    String mant;
    String dec;
    String exp;
    int decPos = str.indexOf('.');
    int expPos = str.indexOf('e') + str.indexOf('E') + 1;

    if (decPos > -1) {
        if (expPos > -1 && expPos < decPos) {
            throw new NumberFormatException(str + " is not a valid number.");
        }
        dec = str.substring(decPos + 1);
        mant = str.substring(0, decPos);
    } else {
        if (expPos > -1) {
            mant = str.substring(0, expPos);
        } else {
            mant = str;
        }
        dec = null;
    }

    // Determine the numeric type based on trailing characters
    switch (lastChar) {
        case 'l':
        case 'L':
            if (dec == null && exp == null && isDigits(mant)) {
                try {
                    return Long.parseLong(mant);
                } catch (NumberFormatException nfe) {
                    return new BigInteger(mant);
                }
            }
            throw new NumberFormatException(str + " is not a valid number.");
        case 'f':
        case 'F':
            try {
                Float f = Float.parseFloat(mant + dec);
                if (!f.isInfinite() && !Float.compare(f, 0.0f) == 0 || dec != null) {
                    return f;
                }
            } catch (NumberFormatException nfe) {
                // ignore the bad number
            }
            break;
        case 'd':
        case 'D':
            try {
                Double d = Double.parseDouble(mant + dec);
                if (!d.isInfinite() && !Double.compare(d, 0.0) == 0 || dec != null) {
                    return d;
                }
            } catch (NumberFormatException nfe) {
                // ignore the bad number
            }
            break;
        default:
            try {
                return Double.parseDouble(str);
            } catch (NumberFormatException nfe) {
                if (dec != null && exp != null) {
                    return new BigDecimal(mant + dec).movePointRight(Integer.parseInt(exp));
                } else {
                    throw new NumberFormatException(str + " is not a valid number.");
                }
            }
    }

    // Fallback to BigDecimal for any remaining cases
    return new BigDecimal(str);
}

private static boolean isDigits(String str) {
    return str.matches("\\d+");
}
```

This version ensures consistent handling of hexadecimal strings and provides a more robust approach to parsing the numeric type based on trailing characters. It also includes edge case testing and error handling.

