public void drawPie(Graphics2D g2, Rectangle2D originalPlotArea, PieDataset dataset, int pieIndex) {
    // Setup plot area and clipping region
    Graphics2D g = (Graphics2D) g2.create();
    g.setClip(originalPlotArea);

    // Calculate angles for each segment
    double totalValue = 0;
    for (Number value : dataset.getValueMap().values()) {
        totalValue += value.doubleValue();
    }

    int sectionCount = dataset.getKeys().size();
    double angleStep = 360.0 / sectionCount;

    // Draw the sides of the pie chart
    for (int i = 0; i < sectionCount; i++) {
        Number value = dataset.getValueMap().get(dataset.getKey(i));
        double angleStart = i * angleStep;
        double angleExtent = value.doubleValue() / totalValue * 360.0;

        Arc2D segment = new Arc2D.Double(originalPlotArea, angleStart, angleExtent, Arc2D.PIE);

        // Fill and outline the segment
        g.setPaint(lookupSectionPaint(dataset.getKey(i)));
        g.fill(segment);
        g.setStroke(lookupSectionOutlineStroke(dataset.getKey(i)));
        g.setColor(lookupSectionOutlinePaint(dataset.getKey(i)));
        g.draw(segment);
    }

    // Draw labels and tooltips (simplified)
    drawLabels(g2, dataset.getKeys(), totalValue, originalPlotArea, null, null);

    // Restore the original clip
    g.dispose();
}
```

This simplified version focuses on drawing the segments and outlines, while leaving the label and tooltip generation to separate methods.

