The `calculateDomainRangeAxes` method is called from within the `draw()` method before any data items are rendered. This ensures that the axes have been drawn and sized before any data items are rendered. 

Here's a simplified version of how it might look:

```java
public AxisState calculateDomainRangeAxes(Graphics2D g2, Rectangle2D plotArea) {
    AxisState state = new AxisState();
    // Reserve space for the domain axis (if any)...
    RectangleEdge domainEdge = Plot.resolveDomainAxisLocation(getDomainAxisLocation(), getOrientation());
    if (domainAxis != null) {
        state = domainAxis.reserveSpace(g2, this, plotArea, domainEdge, state);
    }
    // Reserve space for the range axis (if any)...
    RectangleEdge rangeEdge = Plot.resolveRangeAxisLocation(getRangeAxisLocation(), getOrientation());
    if (rangeAxis != null) {
        state = rangeAxis.reserveSpace(g2, this, plotArea, rangeEdge, state);
    }
    return state;
}
```
